=== epam Output (attempt 2) ===
The tests are still failing because the implementation doesn't properly handle Unicode characters and the custom suffix case. Let me fix the truncate.ts implementation to:

1. Properly handle Unicode characters by using String.prototype.codePointAt()
2. Correctly calculate available space when using custom suffixes

Here's the corrected implementation:

```typescript
export function truncate(text: string, maxLength: number, suffix: string = '...'): string {
  if (text.length <= maxLength) return text;
  
  // Calculate available length accounting for suffix
  const availableLength = maxLength - suffix.length;
  
  // If no room for text, return just suffix
  if (availableLength <= 0) return suffix;
  
  // Handle Unicode characters properly by using code points
  let truncated = '';
  let charCount = 0;
  let i = 0;
  
  while (charCount < availableLength && i < text.length) {
    const codePoint = text.codePointAt(i)!;
    truncated += String.fromCodePoint(codePoint);
    charCount++;
    i += codePoint > 0xFFFF ? 2 : 1;
  }
  
  return truncated + suffix;
}
```

